1
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:14,257
Our primary objective this
time around was to find you,

2
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:16,260
Boxxo, and I'm so glad we did.

3
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:18,657
We could head back but I have a proposal.

4
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:20,357
There's something that might
be worth sticking around

5
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:23,097
the Labyrinth Stratum a bit
longer for if you're game.

6
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:24,010
If I'm game?

7
00:00:24,093 --> 00:00:27,157
Now, this mission came as a humble
request from the Menagerie of Fools.

8
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:30,337
They want our help in defeating
the Skeletitan of Stratumlord.

9
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,302
He's the one we ran into before.

10
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,517
We weren't considering
defeating it originally.

11
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:39,040
But it does present a danger
to hunters if left unchecked.

12
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:45,680
So, bearing that in mind, I for one feel
it's my duty to help them if possible.

13
00:00:46,260 --> 00:00:48,436
Director Bear is a consummate leader.

14
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:53,096
I imagine it'd be prudent to let the
Menagerie make their case as well.

15
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:56,592
He said it, but I like explaining things.

16
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:58,957
Yeah, we want to defeat
this Stratumlord guy.

17
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:02,557
And we think that with your help,
we've got a fighting chance.

18
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,540
But, like, have you met the guy?

19
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:07,637
Look, I get that it's
a big-time undertaking.

20
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:10,297
But since I love explaining,
I'll tell you this too.

21
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:13,677
Every member of the Menagerie
of Fools has a personal goal.

22
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:17,137
We're resolute about achieving
these goals, no matter the cost.

23
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:19,677
Even if that means people
treat us like fools,

24
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:22,936
calling us a menagerie as
if we're a bunch of animals.

25
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,417
Tell me something, Boxo.

26
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,517
Have you heard the
legend of the labyrinth?

27
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:27,430
Too bad.

28
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:32,317
It holds that anyone who reaches the
dungeon, the labyrinth's lowest level,

29
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:34,257
and manages to meet its requirements,

30
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:36,399
will be granted any wish they make.

31
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,348
That sounds pretty awesome.

32
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:40,130
Hmm.

33
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,097
Thank you

34
00:02:02,180 --> 00:02:09,180
so

35
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:19,180
much for watching.

36
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:52,257
Thank you.

37
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:53,440
I'm proud of you,

38
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,360
I'm proud of you,

39
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:09,620
I'm proud of you,

40
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:13,797
People may have reached the lowest level,

41
00:03:13,880 --> 00:03:16,797
but to this day, no one has
conquered the dungeon yet.

42
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,174
No one knows what the requirements are.

43
00:03:19,540 --> 00:03:21,277
That's what we're after, Boxo.

44
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:23,125
Thanks for letting me explain.

45
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:24,439
Requirements, huh?

46
00:03:24,780 --> 00:03:27,877
Rumor is there's not so little
catch about those wishes.

47
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:30,117
Seems they can only be granted
if you have one of those

48
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:33,037
coins that drops when you
take down a Stratum Lord.

49
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:33,950
Wait a sec.

50
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:37,277
Like the eight-legged crocodile
coin I have in my inventory?

51
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:39,184
Who knew it was worth all that?

52
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:43,906
You know that the Menagerie of
Fools consists of eight members.

53
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:45,726
The twins have the same wish.

54
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:50,357
The vice captain and I also share
one, so that makes six wishes total.

55
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:53,297
We've already got three
of those coins between us.

56
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:54,615
Half of what we need.

57
00:03:54,880 --> 00:03:57,821
So I could use my coin to
have a wish granted too?

58
00:03:58,320 --> 00:04:01,657
Maybe I should become a super
high-performance vending machine.

59
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:02,975
Or not, I don't know.

60
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:04,860
And according to Hulemy,

61
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:09,157
you've got a human soul buried
somewhere in that Boxxo body of yours.

62
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:10,377
If you work with us,

63
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:14,217
I don't see any reason you couldn't
put that soul back into a human body.

64
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:15,200
Huh? For real?

65
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:17,717
Don't tease, you mean it?

66
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:22,297
Yeah, I remember stumbling across a situation
like that in a book once upon a time.

67
00:04:22,380 --> 00:04:24,300
So, Boxxo in human form, huh?

68
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:26,587
You could even win a reward!

69
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,620
Appreciate the save there, Boxxo.

70
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:34,717
Regardless, we gotta get to the lowest
level before we'll get any wishes.

71
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:36,540
So, to beef up our abilities,

72
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:41,077
we're hitting all the strata, keeping
ears to the ground for news about lords,

73
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,997
finding them, and taking them out.

74
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,537
Which brings me to this.

75
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:47,117
When you defeated the
eight-legged crocodile,

76
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:49,217
did one of those coins I mentioned appear?

77
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:50,130
Hello there!

78
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:51,670
I see.

79
00:04:51,780 --> 00:04:53,737
And do you have it on you right now?

80
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:54,660
Hello there!

81
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:56,770
I'll be.

82
00:04:56,853 --> 00:04:58,662
Best news I've heard in a while.

83
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:02,667
Suboxo Lamas, you're officially
invited to join the Menagerie.

84
00:05:03,180 --> 00:05:06,697
I mean, you don't have to sign
on for every quest or anything.

85
00:05:06,780 --> 00:05:10,797
But you're welcome to work with us on
campaigns when we need some extra help.

86
00:05:10,880 --> 00:05:12,620
I'm in, but what about Lamas?

87
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,192
Hmm, sounds like a plan.

88
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:16,937
Then we could talk for real.

89
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:19,314
And you could even try my cooking, too.

90
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:21,000
Fine, twist my arm.

91
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,497
I'll work with you, too.

92
00:05:22,580 --> 00:05:23,521
Glad to hear it.

93
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:25,700
So, Boxo, what do you say?

94
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,782
Want to join this ship of fools?

95
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:29,650
Hello there.

96
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,560
Heck yes, Boxo.

97
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:33,309
This is the best day ever.

98
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:37,837
And with Boxo along for the ride, we'll
never have to worry about food, either.

99
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:41,155
The thought of campaigning
just got a whole lot better.

100
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:44,300
Back to being human? Huh.

101
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:58,332
If I had a human body, I could
probably feel their warmth.

102
00:05:58,420 --> 00:05:59,600
That would be nice.

103
00:06:03,080 --> 00:06:05,857
Well, don't you all look
prepped and ready to go?

104
00:06:05,940 --> 00:06:08,117
How about we get our bearings, shall we?

105
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,280
No pun intended.

106
00:06:09,780 --> 00:06:11,060
That's the new map?

107
00:06:11,260 --> 00:06:14,037
I couldn't call that
accurate even to be polite.

108
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:17,737
If only I could share my security
camera images with him somehow.

109
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:19,585
Oh, I could use this function.

110
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:23,400
Show up.

111
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:32,237
Is that...

112
00:06:32,320 --> 00:06:34,240
Yes, the labyrinth stratum.

113
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:36,340
Boxo, how'd you get this?

114
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:37,970
Interesting.

115
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:42,422
Boxxo, are you somehow able to
show us all the things you've seen?

116
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:43,620
Hello there!

117
00:06:44,520 --> 00:06:46,814
That's quite an impressive feat, Boxxo.

118
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,353
Guess who's getting a bonus
from the Hunters Association?

119
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:52,200
Demon, please.

120
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:53,641
Coming right up.

121
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:57,465
I hope this makes the
approach a little easier.

122
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:02,920
Now, how to defeat the Stratum
Lord, the Flame Skelet Titan?

123
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:07,757
Just up ahead of us, there's a rather
sizable trap waiting to be sprung,

124
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:12,060
but it only activates under very
specific conditions. Let me guess.

125
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,477
Those are weight-related.

126
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,390
That's right.

127
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:17,337
Anything above a certain weight
will trigger the trap's door,

128
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:19,857
which opens to a cavernous
hole in the ground.

129
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:24,357
We once tried to march a large group through
this stratum and paid the price for it.

130
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:28,457
As you might have surmised, we'll drop
the Flameskeletitan into that hole.

131
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,797
A hole big enough for
that thing to fit into?

132
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:31,880
Cavernous indeed.

133
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:34,277
How exactly do you plan to get a stratum,

134
00:07:34,360 --> 00:07:36,477
Lord, to fall for a
trap in its own stratum?

135
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:38,619
We'll use its expertise against it.

136
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:41,917
If the Skeletitan won't
activate the trap on its own,

137
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
we'll just have to do it manually.

138
00:07:44,180 --> 00:07:48,297
I guess that's why we put this campaign
group together with quality over quantity,

139
00:07:48,380 --> 00:07:49,210
Amai.

140
00:07:49,293 --> 00:07:50,123
Aha!

141
00:07:50,206 --> 00:07:52,097
Now I understand why
Karyos and Gorth are here.

142
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:55,533
These two are a lot more
skilled than your average guard.

143
00:07:57,020 --> 00:08:00,079
Alright, everyone, stay
close to the left-hand wall.

144
00:08:00,260 --> 00:08:02,540
By close, I mean backs up against it.

145
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:16,320
Look closely now.

146
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:19,920
Make sure you take in the
exact placement of the hole.

147
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:26,111
Right, time for my favorite
thing, a detail of explanation.

148
00:08:26,520 --> 00:08:30,108
The hole is over twice as deep
as the flame skeleton is tall.

149
00:08:30,520 --> 00:08:33,957
We plan to lure it to right on top
of the hole and let it fall in.

150
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:37,657
But even if that works, we doubt
it'll be enough to finish it off.

151
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:38,960
Okay, so then what?

152
00:08:39,060 --> 00:08:40,677
Are we gonna attack it from up here?

153
00:08:40,760 --> 00:08:42,360
Of course. Thing is,

154
00:08:42,620 --> 00:08:44,317
even if we attack from above,

155
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:47,617
the fire all over its body will
melt everything we throw at it.

156
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:50,937
That's why I'm thinking we could make
use of the Vice Captain's water magic,

157
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:52,757
combined with some water from Box Hill.

158
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:56,240
Fill the hole before we dump
the big fiery guy in. I see.

159
00:08:56,660 --> 00:08:59,013
So the plan is to extinguish the flames,

160
00:08:59,160 --> 00:09:01,677
exposing the bone like we
would with flame skulls,

161
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:04,348
and then inflict as
much damage as possible.

162
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:05,570
Voxo,

163
00:09:05,653 --> 00:09:07,537
is it even possible to
sell or dispense enough

164
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:10,057
water to implement the
plan we're proposing?

165
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:15,000
I can dispense bottled water, but it'll
take days to dispense enough to do that.

166
00:09:21,120 --> 00:09:21,950
Dang it!

167
00:09:22,080 --> 00:09:25,177
A vending machine's sole purpose
is to provide for its customers!

168
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:26,436
I'll add a function.

169
00:09:31,620 --> 00:09:35,177
Well, that's yet another shape
I've never seen Boxo make before.

170
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:38,657
So, I take it we can interpret
this change as your answer, Boxo?

171
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:39,570
Hello there!

172
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:42,580
So there are multiple extensions now,

173
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:45,997
which leads me to believe each of them
serves a different function when you push it?

174
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:48,617
much like punching in different
numbers to buy different items.

175
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:50,406
There are some pictures here.

176
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:52,700
Maybe they tell you how to use it.

177
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,300
Let's see.

178
00:09:55,280 --> 00:09:58,980
Squeeze this lever and it will
dispense water. Hello there.

179
00:09:59,440 --> 00:10:00,740
Please insert coins.

180
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:02,932
You're up, Vice Captain.

181
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:03,870
Thank you, Captain.

182
00:10:03,953 --> 00:10:08,606
I so enjoy you ordering me to pay for
things when you never open your own purse.

183
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,340
Okay, folks, ready for blast-off.

184
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:17,290
Whoa!

185
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:23,700
This is great!

186
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:27,517
That could easily extinguish
a flame skull, no problem.

187
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:30,917
With that rate of flow, filling the
hole will take days, but it'll work.

188
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,660
You're a lifesaver, Boxo.

189
00:10:34,780 --> 00:10:37,440
Sure, but there's just one little problem.

190
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:39,360
I can change forms.

191
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:42,834
but I can only maintain the
new one for two hours a day.

192
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,100
What a pain.

193
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:48,505
It's been two days since then.

194
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:53,156
For just one hour each day, I turn
into a power washer and spray water.

195
00:10:53,800 --> 00:10:56,597
At other times, I have them
throw in bottled water.

196
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:59,856
Once it's been thrown, I do
away with all the bottles.

197
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:04,937
Things like huge hog fiends and flame
skulls have shown up several times,

198
00:11:05,020 --> 00:11:08,196
but they're no threat for a
group of this skill level.

199
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,871
When flame skulls appear,

200
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:14,697
Llamas puts me on her back
and Shui gleefully douses

201
00:11:14,780 --> 00:11:17,662
the fiery foes with the
sprayer to take them out.

202
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:23,377
Right, time to find out
how much water's collected.

203
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:25,754
Keep a firm grip on the lifeline, okay?

204
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:32,000
Wow, didn't expect it to be as
cold as midwinter down here.

205
00:11:32,260 --> 00:11:35,437
Looks like this ground drains
better than we anticipated.

206
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:38,277
It hasn't collected at
all. I see. Now what?

207
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:41,536
It was a good plan, but we're
going to have to modify.

208
00:11:41,880 --> 00:11:45,617
Dropping it in the pit should still
work, but as for the rest of the plan,

209
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:47,320
it needs massaging.

210
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:49,113
Good drainage, you say?

211
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:50,500
I've got this.

212
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:54,170
Boxo?

213
00:11:54,253 --> 00:11:56,413
Wait, does this mean you've got an idea?

214
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:59,640
Hey now, I see where you're headed.

215
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:04,175
Since it's so cold down there, we can
fill it with ice instead of water.

216
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:09,997
My speed has increased, so I'm able
to produce the ice cubes much faster.

217
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:12,097
But I don't know, I'm skeptical.

218
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:16,180
Is an ice water bath going to be
enough to defeat the stratum horde?

219
00:12:31,260 --> 00:12:33,237
Hey, Boxo, what you thinking about?

220
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:35,380
Something I can help you with? Huh?

221
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:36,760
How can you tell?

222
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:40,857
I don't know if you've noticed
or not, but when you're thinking,

223
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:42,822
your lighting flickers a little.

224
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:44,380
Wow, it does?

225
00:12:44,820 --> 00:12:46,740
Voxo, can I ask you something?

226
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:48,160
Hello there!

227
00:12:48,420 --> 00:12:51,160
Do you even actually
want to be human again?

228
00:12:53,060 --> 00:12:56,531
Anyone else would think that's
a no-brainer, but not Lamas.

229
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:57,934
She knows me too well.

230
00:12:58,300 --> 00:12:59,717
At first, I did want that.

231
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:03,859
I guess I would enjoy being able to
have real conversations with her.

232
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:07,460
But still, a scary thought haunts me.

233
00:13:08,040 --> 00:13:11,417
If I weren't a vending machine,
would my friends still value me?

234
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:13,265
What would I be worth to them?

235
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:17,037
Right now, my sense of value is clear
because of all I can do for them.

236
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:19,238
But if I went back to being human...

237
00:13:21,840 --> 00:13:22,670
Boxo?

238
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:25,757
Don't get me wrong, I'm sure
they'd be happy at first.

239
00:13:25,840 --> 00:13:28,297
But once they saw what they'd
lost by my transformation,

240
00:13:28,380 --> 00:13:31,968
they might start wishing I was
still a magic vending machine.

241
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:34,947
Not gonna lie, thoughts
like that terrify me.

242
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:38,057
That's why I can't bring myself
to acquire the telepathy function,

243
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:39,757
no matter how it might help.

244
00:13:39,840 --> 00:13:41,120
How pathetic is that?

245
00:13:41,880 --> 00:13:46,174
What sad sack soul has more confidence
as a vending machine than a human?

246
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:48,440
Hello there. Too bad.

247
00:13:49,100 --> 00:13:49,930
Hmm?

248
00:13:50,013 --> 00:13:51,557
Does that mean that you're not sure?

249
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:56,177
Times like these make me wish we could
talk about all kinds of things, you know?

250
00:13:56,260 --> 00:14:00,460
Oh, and like I said before, I
really want you to try my cooking.

251
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:02,900
She's right.

252
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:06,880
I will be human again, and Lamas
and I will walk hand in hand.

253
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:09,440
Maybe that alone is enough.

254
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:14,889
Several more days went by.

255
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:18,137
The pits collected quite a bit of ice,

256
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:21,102
so it's finally time to
put the plan into motion.

257
00:14:22,160 --> 00:14:24,940
Boxo, how do you think
things look, honestly?

258
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:27,834
Does the plan have a chance of success?

259
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:29,680
Hello there!

260
00:14:30,180 --> 00:14:31,709
You seem pretty confident.

261
00:14:32,280 --> 00:14:35,633
The Flame Skeletiton's fire
can vaporize water instantly.

262
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:38,680
I just wonder if ice
is going to be enough.

263
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:41,460
You could even win a reward!

264
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:10,080
Do it, McTenay! Now! Yes, sir!

265
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,620
The reaction will release a
rush of steam, so watch out!

266
00:15:23,360 --> 00:15:24,190
Huh?

267
00:15:24,940 --> 00:15:27,234
The water should have vaporized by now.

268
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:28,340
What's happening?

269
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:29,970
Hang on!

270
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:32,580
The skeleton's fire! It went out!

271
00:15:32,960 --> 00:15:36,217
I don't know what went down,
but if the fire's out, it's out.

272
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:37,653
Time to start throwing!

273
00:15:37,840 --> 00:15:40,840
The flames were extinguished,
but there's no steam?

274
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:43,340
I'm the only one who knows why.

275
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:46,697
What I was chucking into
the hole wasn't ice at all.

276
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:51,280
It was dry ice, and dry ice is
essentially solidified carbon dioxide.

277
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:56,237
So when the flame's skeleton fell in,
the hole filled with carbon dioxide gas.

278
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,144
Fire can't burn without oxygen!

279
00:15:58,340 --> 00:16:00,257
and carbon dioxide collects at the bottom?

280
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,917
since it's heavier than oxygen.

281
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,157
In other words, it put out the flames.

282
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:08,717
It's a good thing my plan worked, because
if it had failed, we'd have been screwed.

283
00:16:08,800 --> 00:16:10,800
Mikenne, how's it look down there?

284
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:13,477
It looks like it's taking
a fair amount of damage,

285
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:14,697
but we're gonna need to hit harder!

286
00:16:14,780 --> 00:16:16,777
if we want this to be over anytime soon.

287
00:16:16,860 --> 00:16:18,978
I wonder how we could hit it harder.

288
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:21,440
It'd take something big and heavy.

289
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:23,060
Something sturdy.

290
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:24,550
Huh?

291
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:28,237
Boxo would make the perfect
weapon in this case.

292
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:31,777
But if it doesn't work, he might
break or even be totally destroyed.

293
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:34,717
He was fine after falling
through a stratum split.

294
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:37,000
That was worse than this. Uh,

295
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:39,377
can you guys stop talking
about doing something

296
00:16:39,460 --> 00:16:42,107
so dangerous with me
like I'm not right here?

297
00:16:42,340 --> 00:16:43,280
Not happening!

298
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,920
We can't force Boxo into danger!

299
00:16:46,340 --> 00:16:48,497
Especially since there's
a chance it won't work.

300
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:49,960
So I vote no, too.

301
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,457
Yeah, you're right.

302
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:54,620
and it'd be cruel to put
any further burden on them.

303
00:16:55,140 --> 00:16:57,197
Shall we jump in and rush the thing?

304
00:16:57,280 --> 00:17:00,120
With the flames
extinguished, we could win.

305
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:04,595
The pit is full of carbon dioxide gas.

306
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,737
Go down there and you
won't have enough oxygen.

307
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:09,097
You will all die of
carbon dioxide poisoning.

308
00:17:12,020 --> 00:17:13,314
Oh, seems Boxo agrees.

309
00:17:14,120 --> 00:17:15,000
I don't!

310
00:17:19,740 --> 00:17:21,560
But we have to do something.

311
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,077
The Flame Skeletiton's trying
to climb out of the hole!

312
00:17:25,160 --> 00:17:27,817
Look, we can't afford to
miss this opportunity.

313
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:29,724
Are you guys ready to win this?

314
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:30,760
This is bad.

315
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,457
If I don't act fast, my
friends could all die.

316
00:17:33,540 --> 00:17:35,357
There has to be some way to stop them.

317
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:36,270
I know!

318
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:39,730
Huh?

319
00:17:39,860 --> 00:17:42,154
Boxo, why are you changing forms again?

320
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,360
Hello there.

321
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:46,917
Please insert coins.

322
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:47,877
Hey, stop that, Boxo!

323
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:50,077
Nobody needs stuff like that right now!

324
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:52,000
Don't be a pervert, jeez!

325
00:17:52,960 --> 00:17:55,400
Oh no, I messed up!

326
00:17:55,780 --> 00:17:57,260
Thank you very much!

327
00:17:57,900 --> 00:17:58,730
Help!

328
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:00,180
Watch out!

329
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:09,680
12 damage.

330
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:12,060
Durability has been decreased by 12.

331
00:18:24,180 --> 00:18:26,415
Looks like I managed to finish it off.

332
00:18:26,720 --> 00:18:28,426
That means everything's okay.

333
00:18:29,140 --> 00:18:29,970
Boxo!

334
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,740
That was so reckless!

335
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:33,300
Hold on a minute!

336
00:18:33,480 --> 00:18:35,068
I'm coming down to get you!

337
00:18:35,920 --> 00:18:39,860
Too bad.

338
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,720
Too bad. Too bad.

339
00:18:43,360 --> 00:18:44,190
Boxo!

340
00:18:44,273 --> 00:18:47,572
Are you trying to tell us it's
still dangerous down there?

341
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:48,790
Hello there!

342
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,190
There!

343
00:18:57,260 --> 00:19:00,789
Flame's Skeletitan coin was
added to my list of possessions.

344
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:23,680
Oh, Mickey, shut the hole, quickly.

345
00:19:24,260 --> 00:19:25,180
You got it.

346
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,080
Boxo! Huh?

347
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:42,237
What would we have done
if you had broken, huh?

348
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:43,897
You could even win a reward.

349
00:19:43,980 --> 00:19:44,977
Don't give me that.

350
00:19:45,060 --> 00:19:46,897
I gotta say, I'm mad at you, Boxo.

351
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:49,509
Come on, cut the guy
a little slack, Lamas.

352
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:53,257
No sense punishing a friend for a good
deed, unless you want him to be mad at you.

353
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,170
But I...

354
00:19:54,253 --> 00:19:55,083
Fine, I'll drop it.

355
00:19:55,166 --> 00:19:56,807
I'm just mad because I care.

356
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:59,158
No more crazy stunts like that, Kay.

357
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:01,960
I didn't answer yes or no.

358
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:05,497
If it meant saving everyone,
I'd do it again and again.

359
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:10,109
And I didn't want to make a promise I
couldn't keep, especially not to Lamas.

360
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:15,520
And then, she smiled an
exasperated smile at me.

361
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:19,637
You guys done talking
because I have an important

362
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:23,697
question for you tell me
did the stratum lord's coin

363
00:20:23,780 --> 00:20:26,737
happen to drop while you
were down in that hole hello

364
00:20:26,820 --> 00:20:30,177
there oh you even picked it

365
00:20:30,260 --> 00:20:34,017
up for me how kind hold on

366
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:36,677
what's the big idea hula
me you're trying to claim

367
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:39,857
the reward like there's no
question that it's yours but

368
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:43,137
boxo defeated the flame
skeleton which means you're

369
00:20:43,220 --> 00:20:47,477
not the rightful owner of
this coin sorry guess you're

370
00:20:47,560 --> 00:20:50,197
right about that it'd be
wrong to deny that everything

371
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:53,037
worked out because of your
exploits box so you were

372
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:55,157
in this coin fair and square
with your heroics and I

373
00:20:55,240 --> 00:20:57,657
would never take that right
from you so how about this

374
00:20:57,740 --> 00:21:00,717
let me buy it off you how
does a hundred gold coin

375
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:05,197
sound did he say a hundred
gold coins converted into

376
00:21:05,280 --> 00:21:08,737
points that's a hundred
thousand heck yes you can't

377
00:21:08,820 --> 00:21:11,797
hmm that's about the going
right for stratum lord coin?

378
00:21:11,880 --> 00:21:14,597
so I can vouch that he's
offering you a square deal.

379
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:17,060
You heard him, Boxo. What'll it be?

380
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:21,117
Not only is that fair and square,
it's an embarrassment of riches.

381
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:25,277
Plus, I already have one Stratum Lord
coin, so I don't need another one.

382
00:21:25,360 --> 00:21:26,190
Hello there.

383
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:30,584
I knew you'd agree, Boxo, but I'm
glad you didn't waste any time.

384
00:21:30,700 --> 00:21:32,137
You mind if I pay you another day?

385
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:34,632
I'm a little bit cash poor at the moment.

386
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:37,336
Well done, everyone.

387
00:21:37,940 --> 00:21:39,116
Let's head for home.

388
00:21:43,700 --> 00:21:47,580
Alright, now for the journey back
to the Clear Flow Lake Stratum.

389
00:21:50,860 --> 00:21:52,997
Looks like all I'll get
to see at the Labyrinth

390
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:56,315
Stratum is the view from the
sky in these main avenues.

391
00:21:57,620 --> 00:22:00,208
Yeah, I probably won't
see this place again.

392
00:22:19,020 --> 00:22:20,317
I'll

393
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:26,917
see you

394
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,020
next time.

395
00:22:42,420 --> 00:22:47,680
I don't know, but this moment I'm happy.

396
00:22:49,560 --> 00:22:51,900
Today is a good day.

397
00:22:53,220 --> 00:23:06,097
I'm always hungry.

398
00:23:36,100 --> 00:23:36,930
much.

399
00:23:37,060 --> 00:23:39,178
I look forward to serving you again.
